{"actions": [{"action_type": "openUrl", "label": "Track weekly caps", "required": true, "target": "https://www.consumer.gov/managing-your-money/making-budget"}, {"action_type": "openUrl", "label": "Subscription audit", "required": true, "target": "https://www.usa.gov/money-tools"}], "code_blocks": [], "content_units": ["Monthly Budget Snapshot", "You bring home   $3,850/month   and currently spend   $3,910/month  , so your budget is running at about   -$60/month   before any extra surprises.", "That means to free up   $250/month  , you actually need about   $310/month in total improvement  :", "-   $60   to stop the current shortfall", "-   $250   to create the extra room you want", "Cut Plan to Free Up $310+", "Category   Current   Suggested   Monthly Change", "Eating out   $310   $180     +$130", "Subscriptions   $72   $18     +$54", "Miscellaneous shopping   $260   $160     +$100", "Entertainment   $190   $140     +$50", "Groceries   $520   $480     +$40", "Gym   $48   $48   $0", "Total improvement             +$374", "This plan would move you from   -$60/month   to about   +$314/month  , which clears your goal.", "Best Places to Cut Without Touching Rent or Insurance", "1) Eating out", "You want to keep   one restaurant meal per week  , so the category should stay — just shrink.", "- Current:   $310", "- Target:   $180", "- Cut:   $130", "Why this works:", "- $180/month is about   $45/week", "- That supports   one modest restaurant meal each week", "- Shift any extra takeout/coffees/snacks into groceries", "2) Subscriptions", "You want to keep   one streaming service  , so trim the rest.", "- Current:   $72", "- Target:   $18", "- Cut:   $54", "Good rule:", "- Keep   1 streaming service", "- Cancel or pause everything else you do not use weekly", "3) Miscellaneous shopping", "This is one of the easiest flexible categories to tighten.", "- Current:   $260", "- Target:   $160", "- Cut:   $100", "How:", "- Put a hard cap on impulse purchases", "- Delay nonessential